    <fr:title text="(Q-MOD): the reductive repair">(Q-MOD): the reductive repair</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result 12 (the reductive repair).</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>(Q-MOD). <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link> is equivalent to <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {mod}(Q : \mathfrak {n}_{c}) \le  \operatorname {umod}(c'),
  \qquad 
  Q = U(L) \times  \mathrm {GL}(W) \times  U(R) \ltimes  N.
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Pass to a generic element and split off the reductive factor.
The exact <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex>-equivariant fibration then makes (Q-MOD) equivalent to
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T_1 + T_2 \le  \operatorname {mod}(A : B)]]></fr:tex>, where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T_1]]></fr:tex> is a rank-<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v]]></fr:tex>
determinantal modality. A bonus of the repair is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_q() = z_u()]]></fr:tex>, which
is what turns the orbit ledger into <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link> in the first
place.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Measured: 807 shapes, slack 0. The equivalence is proven; it has
not closed <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> The naive <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[LK_s]]></fr:tex> ledger is wrong. The exact coupling is
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {V}_0^{\mathrm {Ext}} - v^2 = LK_z - LK_s]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:link>.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
