            <fr:title text="Tall-Lemma V">Tall-Lemma V</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">result13_addendum.md 13(f)--(l); ns_theta.log, tall_exact2.py and .log, dip_exact.py and .log. Note tall_exact2, dip_exact and ns_session_state were lost pre-commit and regenerated from umod_tables.tsv, reproducing the cited numbers exactly.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For every <html:em>tall</html:em> split, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> holds with equality.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Zero violations in 11,452 tall splits, against 958 failures all
of which are off-tall (tall_exact2.log).</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Tallness is exactly the scope, and the three cases say why.
Dominated splits carry the gain in the kernel of the fibration map
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Theta ]]></fr:tex>, where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  \ker  \Theta  = v^2]]></fr:tex>; tall-not-dominated carry it
in the image; off-tall breaks the balance by exactly <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[+1]]></fr:tex>, an S-mode
through <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ker  \alpha ]]></fr:tex>. The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex>-fibration machinery of
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0047/" title="(Q-MOD): the reductive repair" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0047/" display-uri="ffi-0047" type="local">(Q-MOD)</fr:link> consumes precisely tallness and nothing more.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
